# Review ownership. Required by code-review-gate --architecture-only, which
# resolves the approvers for the architecture layer from this file.
#
# Two owners on one line, on purpose. GitHub never requests a review from the
# pull request author (the API rejects it with 422 "Review cannot be requested
# from pull request author"), so a single-owner line requests nobody whenever
# that owner is the one opening the PR. With both listed, whichever one authors
# the PR, the other is auto-requested. Any one approval satisfies the rule.
#
# @alexxo is the same human as @abecerriltrazodigital (personal vs. Trazodigital
# account). Only the org account is listed: adding both would let one person
# satisfy the four-eyes rule alone.
#
# USER_MANUAL.md § 9.4 declares three architecture-owned paths, not one. The
# tech-stack files are human-owned configuration (AGENTS.md § "Ownership
# boundaries" forbids the agent from editing them), so a change there is an
# architecture decision and needs the same approval as docs/architecture/.
docs/architecture/       @MFei8ht @abecerriltrazodigital
tech-stack.yaml          @MFei8ht @abecerriltrazodigital
tech-stack-integrations/ @MFei8ht @abecerriltrazodigital
